@model ErrorViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Something went wrong";
}

<h1>Something went wrong</h1>

<p>
    The portal could not complete that request. Nothing was changed by the
    attempt that failed.
</p>

@if (Model.ShowRequestId)
{
    <p>
        If you report this, quote the reference below. It identifies the failure
        in the server log.
    </p>

    <p><strong>Reference:</strong> <code>@Model.RequestId</code></p>
}

<p><a href="/">Return to the dashboard</a></p>

@*
    Deliberately says nothing about the failure itself. The template this file
    replaced printed advice to "swap to the Development environment to display
    more detailed information about the error", which tells whoever hit the page
    how to make the server disclose more, and reads as a developer note to an
    employee. Claude.md §34 keeps stack traces, SQL errors, class names and
    infrastructure detail off the response; the reference above is how the two
    ends are joined instead.
*@
